      "content": "Cancellation can still return `Rejected` before candidate creation. For example, if the signal aborts while `host.estimate()` is pending and the estimate reports insufficient capacity, the earlier return bypasses this abort check. Similarly, aborting during the initial header read can return a read/format rejection. Check the signal immediately after these awaited operations, before handling their rejection conditions, so cancellation consistently returns `Cancelled`; close the reader on those cancellation paths as well.",
